# Spydle

A daily deduction game inspired by Wordle. Every day a new case is generated — find the spy hidden among a crowd of characters by interrogating a limited number of suspects.

## Gameplay

A crowd of 64 procedurally generated characters is displayed. One of them is the spy. The player interrogates suspects and presents them to an off-screen informant, who answers yes or no depending on whether the selected character shares a trait with the spy. After a limited number of interrogations the player presents a final group of suspects — if the spy is among them, the mission succeeds.

Every player plays the same case each day.

## Architecture

The project is a monorepo consisting of a backend API and a frontend web app.

```
spydle/
    spydle-api/           # ASP.NET Core Web API backend
    spydle-frontend/      # React frontend
    docker-compose.yml
```

### Backend — `spydle-api`

Built with ASP.NET Core and Entity Framework Core targeting PostgreSQL.

**Authentication** is handled by ASP.NET Core Identity with JWT bearer tokens. Endpoints that affect game state require an authenticated user.

**Daily case generation** runs on demand when the first player requests the case for a given day. The case is generated using the date as a deterministic RNG seed. The spy's identity is stored server-side until they've run out of interrogations, at which point the spy is revealed.

**Character encoding** uses a bitmask system where each character's traits are encoded as a single integer. Individual traits are isolated by applying named bitmasks, making trait comparison a simple bitwise AND operation. The same encoding is mirrored on the frontend for decoding characters into visual representations.

**Game logic** is handled entirely server-side. The client sends arrays of character codes to the interrogation endpoint and receives a boolean response — the spy's identity is never exposed to the client until the game concludes.

**Tech stack:**
- ASP.NET Core 10
- Entity Framework Core with Npgsql
- ASP.NET Core Identity
- JWT authentication
- PostgreSQL

### Frontend — `spydle-frontend`

Built with React and TypeScript. The UI shell — navigation, authentication pages, layout — is handled by React with React Router. The game itself is rendered in a Phaser.js canvas embedded as a React component.

**Character rendering** is procedural. Each character is assembled at runtime from layered sprite components — base body, eye sockets, eye&chest fill, age overlay and an outline — with tints applied based on decoded trait values. This allows 64 unique characters to be generated from a small set of reusable assets.

**Tech stack:**
- React 19
- TypeScript
- React Router
- Phaser.js
- Vite

## Running Locally

Prerequisites: [Docker Desktop](https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/)

Clone the repository then start all services:

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

| Service  | URL |
|----------|-----|
| Frontend | http://localhost:3000 |
| API      | http://localhost:8080 |
| Database | localhost:5432 |

The API applies database migrations automatically on startup.